    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "The spacious 3-bedroom duplexes at Old Church offer contemporary living across two thoughtfully designed levels, with generous accommodation ranging from approximately 125–130 sq.m. Designed to maximise natural light and space, these exceptional homes feature an open-plan kitchen, dining and living area, three well-proportioned bedrooms including a spacious master bedroom with en-suite, a family bathroom, and ample storage throughout. Finished to a high specification, each home combines modern comfort, energy efficiency and quality craftsmanship.\r\n\r\nIdeally located beside St. Anne's Church in the heart of Shankill, Old Church places every convenience within easy reach. Shankill DART Station is just an 8–10 minute walk away, offering regular services to Dublin City Centre, Dún Laoghaire, Bray and Greystones, while the nearby N11 and M50 provide excellent road connectivity. Shankill Village is just a short stroll from the development and offers a selection of cafés, restaurants, local retailers, Lidl, Tesco Express and everyday services.\r\n\r\nFamilies are well catered for with a range of highly regarded schools nearby, including St. Anne's National School, Rathmichael Parish National School, St. Gerard's School and Holy Child Killiney. For outdoor enthusiasts, Shankill Beach is approximately a 15-minute walk, while Killiney Beach, Killiney Hill Park and Shanganagh Park are all within a 5–10 minute drive, providing an abundance of coastal walks, woodland trails and recreational amenities.\r\n\r\nCombining generous living spaces with an exceptional South Dublin location, these beautifully designed duplexes offer the perfect balance of contemporary comfort, outstanding connectivity and a relaxed coastal lifestyle."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Prime location in Old Church, Shankill.\r\nBright, spacious and well-presented accommodation.\r\nWalking distance to Shankill Village and DART.\r\nEasy access to the M11, N11 and Dublin City Centre.\r\nClose to beaches, coastal walks and local amenities."
      },
      {
